// Worker replicas that have been waiting more than 10 minutes for a node.
// A dedicated node normally takes up to ~2.5 mins to start from cold. While it
// starts Azure often logs "Maximum Allowed Cores exceeded" (NotTriggerScaleUp)
// even though the replica is placed seconds later, so we alert on the wait
// rather than that message.
ContainerAppSystemLogs
| where isnotempty(JobName) and isnotempty(ReplicaName)
| summarize
    PendingFrom = minif(TimeGenerated, Reason == "AssigningReplicaFailed"),
    PlacedAt = minif(TimeGenerated, Reason == "AssigningReplica")
    by ReplicaName, JobName
| where isnotnull(PendingFrom) and isnull(PlacedAt) and PendingFrom < ago(10m)
